seg-f44d01df7b1c = A signed command applied at a deceived time still misroutes

# text
seg-6497012e401e = A technical note for operators of time-indexed networks: constellations that route, task or hand over by a schedule, where each node acts when its own clock reaches a scheduled instant.

# text
seg-714bce435435 = Abbreviations: GNSS, Global Navigation Satellite System; TPL, timing protection level; PNT, positioning, navigation and timing.

# text
seg-a7208323de1c = The claim

# text
# c1: δ
# c2: T
# c3: T + δ
# c4: |δ|
seg-246715a1c559 = Authenticating control messages, including with post-quantum signatures, proves who sent a message and that it was not altered. It does not prove <b>when the receiver acts on it</b>. A node executes a time-indexed command against its own clock. If that clock has been pulled by <c1/>, a command valid for instant <c2/> runs at true time <c3/>, with every signature intact. Once <c4/> exceeds the slot guard, traffic lands in the wrong slot, a link switches while the other end is still pointed elsewhere, or a handover happens early. The network misroutes, and every integrity check in the command path reports success.

# text
seg-8683f0749042 = Why the clock is the soft target

# text
seg-1af5aea2ef5b = <b>GNSS time is the usual reference, and it is spoofable.</b> A node that disciplines its clock to GNSS inherits whatever time the receiver serves. A spoofer that holds the receiver's own quality flags green can pull that time slowly.

# text
# c1: T + w
seg-354a4c706264 = <b>Freshness checks use the same clock.</b> A validity window ("accept this command until <c1/>") or a replay counter tied to time is judged against the local clock, so a pulled clock can also widen the window in which a captured signed command is accepted.

# text
seg-a4b8a5db0975 = <b>The attack needs no key.</b> Nothing in the signed channel is touched. Stronger cryptography raises the cost of forging a command and leaves this cost unchanged.

# text
seg-e514b03fbae3 = This sits beside post-quantum work, not against it: the two close different holes. Signatures stop a forged command. Time integrity stops a genuine command from being executed at the wrong moment.

